Changed: Tests no longer build their executables while running. In the
deal.II testsuite, all test executables have to be built before invoking
ctest, for example via the new <code>build_tests</code> and
<code>build_tests_&lt;category&gt;</code> targets. The environment variable
TEST_BUILD_REGEX restricts <code>build_tests</code> to the executables of
matching tests. In user projects that use deal_ii_pickup_tests(), a single
setup test "test_dependency/compile_test_executables" builds all test
executables before the tests run (this can be disabled with
TEST_BUILD_FIXTURE). Build failures are still reported per test. Each test
is now run by a single driver program (deal_ii_test_driver) that replaces
the previously used shell, perl, and CMake scripts; bash and perl are no
longer required for running the testsuite. Testsuite subprojects now use
the same CMake generator as the main project.
